From b31fffd8cbe35d470ddaad78362fddd51859e0c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 07:29:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban chat waits: an ask is retried, never written
 passively; answered asks end the streak

Review and adversarial pass of the previous head:
- The once-per-hour budget exemption was charged before routing, so a
  slots-busy pass or a second question within the hour still turned the ask
  into a passive, acked row. The exemption is gone. Instead an ask the sweeper
  cannot wake now (budget spent or slots busy) is handed back and retried each
  pass, the budget still pacing wakes; one undelivered for ASK_OVERDUE_S (2 h)
  goes to David via kanban_decision_ask.escalate (scheduled -> triage ->
  needs_input with the question), the same path as the owner fallback.
- With one premise per orchestrator, separately answered questions escalated
  on the third park. prior_same_premise now ends the streak at a chat park
  whose own comment probe (--after-id N) has a non-system comment after it.
  Unanswered or reworded re-asks still escalate on the third park.

Tests: budget spent and slots busy hand the ask back and wake on a later pass
(no passive row); an ask undelivered for 2 h blocks the card needs_input;
three answered questions park three times without escalating. 55 tests;
16 neighbouring files (403 tests) pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
